From 4d32262db6f6acf60c270c67cebd3f3e63a1a875 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:11:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] cron: a deferred pending restart rerun stays pending
 (held in DarkWake, exempt from one-shot grace)

Follow-up to PR #2364 (a4d31b4651), review 5894674747 nit 1, card t_01a1d5c5d776510c.

Gap: when the draining owner refused a pending restart rerun (defer_unadmitted), _marker kept the
rerun's `at` (so the next attempt is still recognised as the rerun) but _apply re-armed
next_run_at=now. pending_rerun compares next_run_at to marker.at, so it read False: the re-armed
rerun was neither held in a DarkWake (hold_for_wake) nor exempt from the one-shot grace gate
(retire_expired_oneshot), and a one-shot rerun held past ONESHOT_GRACE_SECONDS would be retired.

Fix: the kept marker also records the re-arm instant as `fire_at`; pending_rerun matches
next_run_at against `fire_at` when present, else `at`. `at` keeps its meaning for _skip_reason.

Tests:
- new test_deferred_pending_rerun_stays_held_and_survives_the_oneshot_grace[in 30m, every 120m]:
  defer a pending rerun, assert pending_rerun, held while host_fully_awake() is False, not retired
  past ONESHOT_GRACE_SECONDS, fires on full wake. RED at base 3de04d8928 (2 failed: "the deferred
  rerun is no longer pending"), GREEN at head.
- the `clock` (test_restart_rerun.py) and `home` (test_restart_cut.py) fixtures stub
  host_fully_awake to True, so the pre-existing rerun-is-due tests and
  test_owner_cut_of_a_rerun_that_was_awake_ten_minutes_stops no longer depend on a MacBook's power
  state; dropped the now-unneeded raising=False.
- tests/cron/test_restart_rerun.py + test_restart_cut.py: 80 passed. tests/cron +
  test_messaging_exactly_once + test_session_cron: 2656 passed, 0 failed. scripts/check: 19 ok.
